abstract: "For the N-intertwined mean-field (NIMFA) SIS epidemic model on networks, proofs of the two decay conjectures of Persoons, Sensi, Prasse and Van Mieghem (2024): at or below the epidemic threshold the average infection level is at most 1/(1+t) (time in mean recovery times), and above it the excess over the endemic level, starting from above, obeys the same bound. Extensions to time-varying, heterogeneous-recovery and directed networks and to the expected prevalence of the exact stochastic model; attainment on regular graphs; at the threshold the average decays like kappa(G)/t with an explicit eigenvector constant kappa(G) <= 1; node-wise bounds; unconditional transition-time bounds. Unrefereed candidate; internal AI-assisted review only. Text, data and diagrams CC0-1.0; code MIT."
